 "why": {
  "seatParty": "A party is seated against a reservation. **A walk-in is a waitlist entry first**, which is why addWalkIn resolves elsewhere.",
  "moveTable": "**Moving a party is moving a visit.** The table does not move.",
  "voidOrderItem": "**A void is a whole-order act in this model** \u2014 voiding one line is a modification, and voidOrder scoped to a line is the same operation.",
  "adjustStock": "**Every stock change is a movement.** An adjustment with no movement behind it is a level nobody can reconcile \u2014 the same rule that caught four operations writing a derived table on 20 August.",
  "approveWriteOff": "**One approval mechanism, not one per thing approved.** CF-132 settled this: a write-off, a scenario and an action are all approval requests with a different subject.",
  "takePayment": "The payment path is one path. **A till, a link and a kiosk all reach createPayment.**",
  "splitCheck": "**splitBill already existed and I built splitCheck alongside it on 24 August** \u2014 a duplicate path key, caught by the check added on 18 August for exactly this. **The existing one is better**: it distributes remainders to the minor unit and rejects a split that does not sum, which mine did not.",
  "printBill": "**getBill already existed.** Presentation is a read; printing is a client act.",
  "setModifierOptions": "**createModifierGroup and ModifierGroup already existed** \u2014 caught on 24 August by the duplicate-key check, the second time that day. **The existing schema persists to `fnb.modifier_group + fnb.modifier_option` and is the one the untouched-table audit was pointing at all along.**",
  "archiveProduct": "**A lifecycle transition, not a delete.** `transitionProductLifecycle` already moves a product to retired \u2014 and a product with sales history cannot be removed without rewriting last year.",
  "raiseTransferClaim": "**A claim is a transfer closed short.** `closeTransferShort` already records that the balance will not arrive, which is what a claim against the sending outlet is.",
  "setPriorityWeights": "**Folded into `setKitchenSla` on 24 August.** What pushes a ticket up the rail and how long it may sit are one configuration \u2014 splitting them means two screens to change one behaviour.",
  "recordBatchOutput": "**`completeProductionRun` records what was actually made**, which is batch output. The board named the act; the contract named the run.",
  "getFleetHealth": "**`getWorkstationHealth` built 20 August from the same board pack.** A fleet figure is the per-workstation score aggregated \u2014 a score a manager can sort by, which a heartbeat timestamp is not.",
  "listStationEvents": "**All four audit frames are one operation with a filter.** `listAuditRecords` built 24 August because `platform.audit_record` existed and nothing read it \u2014 `BO-068 Audit Log` had zero operations declared.",
  "setOfflineLimits": "**One offline policy, not three.** `setOfflinePolicy` carries the capabilities, the ceilings and the hours \u2014 the board drew them as three panels because they are three panels.",
  "testPeripheral": "**A test is a heartbeat on demand.** `recordDeviceHeartbeat` with the device named \u2014 a separate test endpoint would report a different truth from the one the fleet view reads.",
  "holdSupplier": "**A hold is a status, not an operation.** `updateSupplier` built 24 August \u2014 a supplier on hold stops appearing in requisitions while their history stays intact, and deactivating one who has delivered for two years must not orphan the receipts.",
  "getTransferManifest": "**The manifest is the transfer.** `getStockTransfer` built 24 August \u2014 a receiving store could accept a delivery it could not open first, and a short delivery answered by two calls is two chances to answer it differently.",
  "scanItem": "**`lookupMerchandise` is the scan.** A barcode, an RFID tag and a typed SKU all resolve the same way \u2014 a separate scan endpoint would report a different truth from the one the catalogue holds.",
  "completeSale": "**`createRetailSale` is the sale.** The board names the act at the end of the basket; the contract names the artefact."
 }
}